ntation</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">D</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"D\"></span><span>by providing a timeline and a mind map</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">E</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"E\"></span><span>by making their notes more evaluative</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1},{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-g3-2","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 25-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Which personal meaning do the students decide to give to each of the following pictures?</p><p>Choose&nbsp;<strong>SIX</strong>&nbsp;answers from the box and write the correct letter,&nbsp;<strong>A-H</strong>, next to Questions.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>Personal meanings</strong></strong></p><p><strong>Pictures</strong></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Falcon (Landseer)</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Fish hawk (Audubon)</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Kingfisher (van Gogh)</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Portrait of William Wells</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Vairumati (Gauguin)</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Portrait of Giovanni de Medici</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">a childhood memory</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">hope for the future</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">fast movement</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">a potential threat</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">the power of colour</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">the continuity of life</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">protection of nature</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"H\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">H.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">a confused attitude to nature</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-16-academic-listening-1-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/13180-cambridge-ielts-16-academic-listening-1-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>Stoicism</strong></strong></p><p>Stoicism is still relevant today because of its <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;appeal.</p><p><strong>Ancient Stoics</strong></p><ul><li>Stoicism was founded over 2,000 years ago in Greece.</li><li>The Stoics’ ideas are surprisingly well known, despite not being intended for <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><strong>Stoic principles</strong></p><ul><li>Happiness could be achieved by leading a virtuous life.</li><li>Controlling emotions was essential.</li><li>Epictetus said that external events cannot be controlled but the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;people make in response can be controlled.</li><li>A Stoic is someone who has a different view on experiences which others would consider as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li></ul><p><strong>The influence of Stoicism</strong></p><ul><li>George Washington organised a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;about Cato to motivate his men.</li><li>The French artist Delacroix was a Stoic.</li><li>Adam Smith’s ideas on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;were influenced by Stoicism.</li><li>Some of today’s political leaders are inspired by the Stoics.</li><li>Cognitive Behaviour Therapy (CBT)</li></ul><p>–&nbsp; the treatment for <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;is based on ideas from Stoicism</p><p>–&nbsp; people learn to base their thinking on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p><ul><li>In business, people benefit from Stoicism by identifying obstacles as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Relevance of Stoicism</strong></p><ul><li>It requires a lot of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;but Stoicism can help people to lead a good life.</li><li>It teaches people that having a strong character is more important than anything else.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-16-academic-listening-1-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-c16-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c16-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"egg","correct_answer_variants":["egg"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13094_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-q2","part_id":"en-c16-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c16-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"tower","correct_answer_variants":["tower"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13094_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-q3","part_id":"en-c16-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c16-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"car","correct_answer_variants":["car"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_13094_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c16-t1-l-q4","part_id":"en-c16-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-c16-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"animals","correct_answer_variants":["animals"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[4],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_a